A||||20||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||Mitsubishi Eclipse 2.0L Turbo swap||||1||
Z||000000||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||01-24-2001||02:01 AM||||I have seen posts regarding GM engine swaps in Fieros.  Most of these have regarded the front wheel drive GM engines and in some cases transmissions.  <P>I know it is EXTREMELY arrogant to suggest this one, but I would like to have a intercooled turbo 2.0L 16valve engine/automatic transmission in my fiero.  They are very powerful and lightweight engines.  Swapping one in for my duke would double the power and reduce weight.  Since this weight is in the rear, weight distribution would approach nuetrality.<P>Okay, now there are some major problems that must be solved.  Wiring is likely to entail two independant harnesses cooperating with each other.  The mitsubishi automatic transmission would have to connect to the rear wheels somehow.  And, custom engine and tranny mounts would have to be made.  I suspect time and money could solve most of these.<P>Here's a question for the experts:<P>Can custom driveaxles be fabricated to connect a Mitsubishi transmission to the rear wheels?  What vendors are available for this type of custom work?<P>Yes, there is something morally wrong with putting a Japanese engine in an American car . . . but have you ever heard the eclipse/talon engine? I would love to have a 200HP 7,000 RPM redline Fiero that sounded like a huge, very angry hair dryer . . .<p>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||TheHans||01-24-2001||02:30 AM||||I love that idea!!<BR>That is probably my favorite engine in my favorite car. You make it and they will come.<BR>ZING&gt;ZING&gt;ZING.. every gear..OH HELL YA!||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||01-24-2001||08:35 AM||||Gee guys I just happen to have a 92 Laser AWD turbo  5sp with 73K miles for sale.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||01-24-2001||09:36 AM||||Why go through all the trouble when you could do a 3.4 turbo, get MUCH better results, for a lot cheaper, and still be able to get GM parts for your car????||||reg||5
Z||000004||pherder||01-24-2001||09:51 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LuckyTheyWereEverMade:<BR><B>I would love to have a 200HP 7,000 RPM redline Fiero that sounded like a huge, very angry hair dryer . . .<P>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 01-24-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>HMMMM????  Sounds like my 2.3L HO Quad 4 that I have in my 88 Coupe <B>EXCEPT</B> I have a red line of 7,500 RPM     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>With the mods I have made (removal of the power steering pump, more efficient exhaust system, and a chip from MantaPart making my red line higher, the speed limits gone, etc.), I should have an engine that is putting out 200 hp with <B>STOCK GM PARTS!!!</B><P>BTW, the chip from MantaParts is really a copy of the Olds Achieva SCX's chip so it TOO is a stock GM Part!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul<BR>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com<BR><p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
