Z||000006||loafer87gt||01-24-2001||10:37 AM||||No offense, but theres not a snowballs chance in hell that a 3.4 Pushrod engine could compare to the 2.0 Mitsu engine!Those things make ungodly amounts of horsepower! I had to laugh when I was reading through some of my old car magazines the other day, Hot Rod magazine had built up a late 90's supercharged Camaro that they wanted to be able to slaughter Ferrari's and Porsche's with, they succeeded, but at the cost of over $65,000 in bolt ons. The car was able to run 11.8 in the quarter using slicks. Hot Rods sister magazine, Super Street, had a Talon project  going on at the same time. They had $20,000 invested in the car, including the cars purchase price. Just for a laugh they put it up againts the Camaro and it walked all over it! The Talon was able to run mid 11's with street tires! It was funny because the Hot Rod guys where saying it was because the Talon was so much lighter, but when they weighed the two cars, the Talon was the heavier of the two at over 3800 lbs!! <P>If someone found a way to swap one of these into the Fiero, I would do it in a second. I love these engines, and I think they would be a blast in a Fiero!||||reg||10
Z||000007||Ralfy9862||01-24-2001||02:32 PM||||Hell ya my bro has a turbo 5spd talon and it kicked my v6 5spd fieros ass. those engines rule and sound good especialy when downshifting. and there really fst off the line and then when the turbo kicks in it throws you back in your seat and they hadle good too.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Oreif||01-24-2001||02:49 PM||||Porsche Boxter S has a 24-valve, 3.2L V-6 (I think it's a flat 6) at 250hp in a mid-engine design. Pushes boxster to 60 in 5.6 seconds! HMM what other "mid-engine" car could this get dumped into?<P>As for axles, I have heard of places that will take 2 axles (Fiero and Mitz for the example) and cut them in half then weld the 2 opposties together. I have only heard of this, If you want to check it out, some things to ask would be:<BR>Does it weaken the amount of HP and torque?<BR>(I would assume so). How accurate is the length? Is it cost effective?<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||GT Bastard||01-24-2001||07:47 PM||||This is total bunk...  The best of them make 210hp and the torque isn't anything special.  A tweaked 3.4 could be built to make that with TONS less work/money.  If that's not good enough, even a smallblock or a 3800 Supercharged would a lot less trouble.  Mitsu trannies have a bad track record for durability too.  Besides, nobody is actually going to do this swap anyways, it's all just theoretical crazy-talk.||||reg||1
Z||000010||88formula||01-24-2001||08:25 PM||||I have to agree with you. A friend on mine has the award Talon with the turbo engine and he runs in the low twelve’s with that car. According to him the shortblock is bullet proof.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||01-24-2001||08:29 PM||||GT Bastard is 100% correct.  The tranny's are very unreliable in those cars.  My brother bought a '98 GS-T and he went through 3 tranny's in the 50k mile warranty period.  He sold it soon after the warranty ran out so he wasn't stuck with another bad tranny.<P>The HP that you can make with those small engines is limited.  You said they souped up a "late 90s supercharged Camaro", what model was this?  I don't know of any factory supercharged Camaro.  How did they manage 65 grand in "bolt ons"??? I mean how good of an ignition system can you really buy??? <BR>And if one car runs mid 11's and the other runs 11.8, thats not really "walking all over it"  What editions were these mags (year/month)??<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||87GT||01-24-2001||08:36 PM||||Keep it original||||reg||1
Z||000013||Rashaam||01-24-2001||08:48 PM||||I was going to do that engine swap in to my 87 GT. The only place that I found to do it was HTD in Toronto, Ont. The owners name is Jim and he was very helpful. His e-mail address is htdinc@hotmail.com if you want to ask someone about it. In the end I decieded to get them to put in a 320hp V8 with 100hp NOS kit cause it was cheaper. I get the car this spring and I can't wait.<BR>GT Bastard: No offence but I own a 90 and 95 Talon Tsi Awd and it doesn't take much to up the power on those 2.0L mitsu engines, but I do agree that a better and cheaper choice would be a GM engine.<p>[This message has been edited by Rashaam (edited 01-24-2001).]||||reg||1
