Z||000015||Smokin87||01-24-2001||09:34 PM||||quote:<BR>--------------------------------------------------------------------------------<BR>Originally posted by LuckyTheyWereEverMade:<BR>I would love to have a 200HP 7,000 RPM redline Fiero that sounded like a huge, very angry hair dryer . . .<BR>[This message has been edited by LuckyTheyWereEverMade (edited 01-24-2001<P><BR>That has got to be one of the funniest quotes yet.  And i know what you mean, cause i have a 93 eclipse, and an 87 fiero gt.  <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fiero_20.jpg"> <BR>Justin Coe||||reg||1
Z||000016||loafer87gt||01-24-2001||09:36 PM||||The Camaro was a '94 Z28 putting out 700 HP using a Vortech supercharger and a built 383 smallblock. This car can be found in January 98 Car Craft magazine. running 1/4 @ 11.68<P>The 1990 GSX was running the 1/4 @11.29 It had a PMS computer system, 20G turbo, Crane ignition, extreme tech aircleaner and 3" exhaust. Stock engine internals. April 98 of Super Street.<P>I don't want to start a flame war between American/Jap engines, I'm just saying that the DSM engines are capable of making an unbelievable amount of power for such a small  displacement.<P>Rashaam: Do you know if Hi-Tech in Toronto has ever done one of these swaps before?||||reg||1
Z||000017||Rashaam||01-24-2001||09:54 PM||||No he hasn't put one in yet but he did some research on it before giving me an answer. I was thinking of swapping in the computer, engine and tranny from a 97 Tsi. But like I said before it was to expensive compared to the V8 swap that he does. Plus my car would have been the first one so that has something to do with the price. R&D I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000018||fiero87||01-25-2001||03:12 AM||||All i can say is i have the utmost respect for the DSM engines.  I have helped and worked with my friend on his 92 AWD many times and everytime we do something it just gets faster.  He must have about 15k in mods done, which includes two turbo upgrades, cams, fuel computer, front mount intercooler..etc.. but there is very little on the street that can run with him.  I believe his best time was an 11.80  And his car is still completely streetable.  Drives it to and from the track and kills the trailer queens.  If somone makes a kit for this engine...i'd be the first on the list to buy one.  BTW..his entire motor is bone stock!  Only bolt on upgrades with the exception of the cams.  I love DSM's, and plan to own one someday!!  But of course i'll still keep the fiero's too.. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000019||Wannabe||01-25-2001||01:06 PM||||I used to own 1st gen Eagle Talon TSi and was always impressed with how easily they make power.  A friend with a '93 with only a cat back exhaust and a k&n air filter ran 14.4 in the 1/4. I later heard from someone who had done a Turbo install on their 2.8 fiero and also ran a 14.4. Interesting. Anyway, the first swap I considered for the Fiero was the 2.0 Mits. It would save about 80 lbs from the  V6 and would happily put out 400 hp. Just the same, after taking a close look at SBC swaps, it looks like the V8 solution will be as good (or better in some ways) and will cost a whole lot less. ||||reg||1
Z||000020||danny boy||01-25-2001||10:53 PM|||| IT HAS BEEN DONE!!!<BR>Ok,a little background...<BR>Obviously I have a Fiero or two.What I also have is a '91 Stealth twin turbo.My friend has a Talon turbo.He also used to have an 86 GT 5sp.Anyway, we talked about this a few times after we both got DSMs.The other day he was on the DSM webring and happened to mention Fiero,and another guy replied about His Fiero.He has a '90 talon motor in it. <BR>   My friends Talon runs low 11's/High 10's.<BR>Show me a Fiero that'll do that(I dont care whats in it) and still get 17mpg.<BR>I'll ask him again about where it is and see if I can get that guy over here.||||reg||4
